B.a04=new A.d7("The Library Map",'Ava found a folded map inside a library book. It showed a winding trail between the shelves. She followed the tiny arrows past history, art, and science. At the end, a note read, "Your next adventure is any book you choose."')
B.a0a=new A.d7("Robot Recess","Our class built a robot from cardboard tubes and shiny paper. We programmed it to wave, turn, and play a cheerful tune. At recess, everyone formed a line to teach the robot a new dance move.")
B.a0l=new A.d7("The Tiny Weather Station","Ben placed a rain cup, a wind ribbon, and a thermometer by the garden. Each morning, he recorded what he saw. After one month, his chart showed that windy days often arrived before rain.")
B.a05=new A.d7("A Surprise for Grandma","Lena mixed flour, sugar, and berries while her brother made a colorful card. They cleaned the kitchen before Grandma arrived. When the door opened, the room filled with smiles and the sweet smell of muffins.")
B.a09=new A.d7("The Creek Cleanup","Our nature club met beside the creek on Saturday. Wearing gloves, we collected paper and empty bottles from the path. By noon, the water sparkled and the trail looked welcoming again.")
B.a07=new A.d7("The Homemade Telescope","Kai joined two cardboard tubes and carefully added simple lenses. That evening, he pointed his telescope toward the bright moon. The view was a little fuzzy, but he could still see dark patches and glowing edges.")
B.a0m=new A.d7("Concert in the Kitchen","A wooden spoon became a drumstick, and an empty container became a drum. Soon, pots chimed and cups kept the beat. Our kitchen concert was noisy, joyful, and over just in time for dinner.")
B.a0n=new A.d7("The Seed Exchange","Each student brought a packet of seeds to school. We traded sunflowers, peas, marigolds, and beans. By spring, every windowsill held a different mix of bright leaves and hopeful buds.")
